+# Stren — Development Guide
+
+## Stack
+- Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19)
+- Supabase (PostgreSQL 17) — project ID `wmcjkhstykgyhtpmlvuw`, region `ap-southeast-1`
+- TypeScript strict mode (no `ignoreBuildErrors`)
+
+## DB Workflow Rule
+
+**ALL database changes — tables, RLS policies, functions/RPCs, indexes — must be authored as files in `supabase/migrations/` and applied via the Supabase MCP tool (`apply_migration`) or Supabase CLI (`supabase db push`).**
+
+- NEVER edit the live schema by hand in the Supabase dashboard.
+- After any schema change, regenerate `lib/database.types.ts` using `generate_typescript_types` MCP tool or `supabase gen types typescript`.
+- Confirm `supabase db diff` (or a query against `supabase_migrations.schema_migrations`) is clean before committing.
+- Every `.rpc()` call in application code must have a matching `CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION` in a committed migration.
+
+## Migration Structure
+```
+supabase/migrations/
+  001_production_baseline.sql   ← full idempotent production schema
+  _archive/                     ← old draft migrations (do not apply)
+```
+
+## Auth Helpers (SECURITY DEFINER)
+- `get_gym_id()` — returns the caller's gym_id
+- `get_user_role()` — returns the caller's role
+- `is_manager()` — returns true for admin/staff/owner
+
+## Supabase Clients
+- `lib/supabase.ts` — browser client
+- `lib/supabase-server.ts` — SSR client (use `getUser()` not `getSession()`)
+- `lib/supabase-admin.ts` — service role (server only)
+
+## Type Safety
+- `lib/database.types.ts` is generated, not hand-edited. Regenerate after schema changes.
+- Use `as YourType` casts on RPC results that return `Json` — define the shape inline or in a local type.
